Wow, I am pretty happy with myself. I don't mean to brag, but I have only
been playing Nethack for about a week and a half now. In fact, I only have
around 50 characters on my highscore list. Yeah, I was spoiled to death, but
it was still pretty hard, and was not without a few huge mistakes and close
calls. It was pretty nervewracking considering this was the first character
I've ever gotten past Medusa. I have to give a lot of credit to itsblah in
#nethack on irc.freenode.org - he was very helpful and gave me a lot of good
tips and help.

Anyway, this was a pretty easy ascension. Off the bat I quickly got to
clevel 5 and dipped for Excalibur. I then hit the mines on dlevel 4, and
found no less than 3 bones piles in the mines. 2 were mine, and 1 was from
Hearse. I grabbed some decent starting equipment from them, including an
Amulet of Reflection from a previous character, a touchstone from the Hearse
bones pile of an Archeologist, and wound up with a ring of teleport and a
ring of teleport control from various bones piles. Somewhere in the mines,
my pet cat hit a level teleport trap, and was never seen again.

I hit Sokoban, and grabbed the bag of holding. From there I dove down until
I hit an aligned altar a dlevel or two after Sokoban. I sacrified to Tyr
until I got my gift of Mjollnir, and I used that for the rest of the game,
enchanting it every time I got the chance.

I dove down farther and got to the quest portal, but was only clevel 12, so
I just kept diving down the dungeon. I hit another bones pile of mine, and
picked up some more decent equipment including a magic lamp (which I used
strictly as a light source). Once I hit Medusa's level I turned around and
headed back to my quest portal after deciding to quaff 2 potions of gain
level. I had never done the quest before, but it proved to be a breeze and
Lord Surtur fell in 3 hits from my +6 Mjollnir.

At that point, I was talking in the #nethack channel about not having very
much AC. From there they told me that I could try to find Fort Ludios and
that it had a ton of money and was a good place to get equipment. I set off,
searching on dlevel 11. I found the portal to Ludios on dlevel 12, and
cleared it easily, racking up a good 40,000 zorkmids I believe. I bought as
much bonus AC protection as I could from that, and wasted about 15,000
trying to get 1 last bonus point that I never got.

I took almost all of the helmets and went to my altar and b/u/c checked
them, and tried them on, since I really needed a better helmet. I found a +3
helmet in there, and it was the helmet I used for the rest of the game (I
enchanted it once after). Then on this newsgroup I saw people talking about
polypiling, and I thought it would be a good idea to polypile a ton of armor
from Ludios to try to get something good. I spent about an hour or so taking
a ton of armor and equipment to my base/altar (don't ask me why). After
polypiling everything about 5 times, I was very disappointed that I really
didn't find anything good. I did manage to get an Hawaiian shirt and an
oilskin cloak that I used for the rest of the game (more on the Hawaiian
shirt later).

>From there I hit Medusa's level, killing her easily with my amulet of
reflection, and a blindfold on "just in case". I dove down to the castle,
and noticed there was a mind flayer of some flavour in the castle. I decided
to genocide them so I wouldn't have to worry about it. I cleared the castle,
grabbed the wand of wishing, and fell down into the Valley of the Dead for
the first time ever.

I dove down quickly with few problems, and found yet another wand of wishing
2 levels below the castle. I hit Juiblex where I had an extremely close
call. He immediately devoured and Sickened me and I was starting to panic. I
hit him a few times and he died, then I tried to #pray to get the sickness
away. Mistake. I angered my god, lost all my bought protection, and to top
it off I had a summoned demon beside me and I was Sick. I did a level
teleport to my stash on dlevel 14. In desperation I tried to #pray again,
and it worked. I took out the demon easy, but not before he summoned another
one or something. I survived that huge, stupid mistake, but not without
losing 9AC points and having no money left at all. I read up a bit on
killing priests, and decided it was in my best interest to kill a priest
I've bought protection off of to get the money back. I got about 1/2 my
money back because I used money on more than one priest, and got a good
chunk of of my AC back.

Halfway through Gehennom I decided it would be a good idea to try out this
"nurse dancing" that I read about. I wished for 2 cursed scrolls of genocide
and let them rip in the first sokoban level. I managed to get around 80-100
more HP from that. I did another round of nurse dancing later on. I also
gained about 12 clevels through the game by eating wraiths and quaffing
potions of gain level.

Around this time someone told me that it would be a good idea to wish for a
spellbook of magic mapping to help in Gehennom. I did so, and as any
experienced player (not me) would know, I didn't even have a chance at being
able to cast it. I was then told that a robe and a helm of brilliance might
help me. I wished for both, and they didn't help at all. So there I wasted 3
wishes for nothing. To top it off, I decided to try enchanting the helm of
brilliance to use, but I forgot to take off my +4 Hawaiian shirt and ended
up disintegrating it. In anger I threw the helm of brilliance in my stash
and never looked at it again.

Anyway, I kept diving through Gehennom and killed Vlad, got the candlestick,
and dove down further. I was scared and happy when I first saw the Wizard of
Yendor, it was cool. I kept diving, and near the bottom of the dungeon I hit
stupid mistake #2. It was very late at night, and I was tired, and I
accidently put an unidentified wand into my bag of holding. Of course I
should have known better, and it ended up being a wand of cancellation and I
lost my bag. I don't even remember was I had in the bag, but I did lose a
ton of potions and scrolls. I luckily managed to find another bag of holding
somewhere in Gehennom.

I finished mapping out Gehennom and found the vibrating square. At this
point I decided to go through the whole dungeon and dig out optimal paths
from each stairway to the other. I realize now that it would be better to do
this as I go along instead of going back to do it after. I went to go get
prepared for killing the Wizard and realized I really had no potions of full
healing left. I screwed around in Gehennom for a while, used a lot of
wands/scrolls of create monster and managed to pick up a nice handful of
potions to use.

I decided to go for it, and I loaded up my pack with everything I thought I
would need, left everything else including all my other artifacts in my
stash, and went down to kill the Wizard. I dropped him fast the first time,
and I believe he came alive right away. I grabbed the book, then level
teleported down to the bottom and performed the little ceremony to open the
way to the priest of Moloch. When I went in, the Wizard appeared and
teleported right beside the priest. I fought my way through and had a pretty
hard time finding the secret door to get to the priest. I got some of my
stuff cursed, and the priest/wizard combo was a little bit tougher than I
anticipated, but I dropped both of them pretty easily. I grabbed the amulet,
waved goodbye to the priest's corpse, and took off.

On my way up through the dungeon, I don't believe I saw the Wizard even once
until after I entered the plains. I stopped on dlevel 14 to check my stash
one last time, and then headed down. When I first entered the Earth Plains
the Wizard appeared and I killed him easily, and grabbed his potion and wand
of digging. I used my Orb of Fate to find the portal and dug my way over
easily.

When I hit the Air Plains I was pretty surprised. Until that point, I really
had no problem with any monsters and never really even watched my HP. On the
Air Plains, although, it was different. I was dropped into low 100's of HP
from the air elementals, and ended up using my first potion of full healing.
I finally fought my way over to the portal and jumped in.

The Fire plains were a lot easier, and the only problem I had was that my
Orb of Fate was out of charges, so I tried a cursed scroll of detect gold.
This didn't help a lot, because there was a good 15-20 piles of gold there.
I used my stashed blessed scroll of charging to fix up my orb, and used it
again. It ended up confusing me and didn't work. I tried a few more times
and I finally got it.

I hit the Water Plains and it was the easiest part so far. The only annoying
part was trying to find the portal with the air bubbles throwing me around
everywhere.

Finally, I was on the Astral Plains. I started out in the lower left corner.
Somewhere in there I ended up blinded, and decided to just keep going since
I had telepathy. I decided to try the left altar first, and right away I met
Death. He was a pretty big wimp, and died easily. When I got to the altar, I
found out it was the chaotic altar, and was pretty mad. I got myself
together and decided to try the middle one. I had to take out Death a few
more times on my way out. Next I met Pestilence. I took him out with a wand
of death, and made my way up to the middle altar. Surprise, it was still the
wrong altar. When I tried to get out, Pestilence got me and made me Ill. I
quickly used a blessed unicorn horn, then blasted him again with a wand of
death. I finally made my way to the last remaining altar, and took out
Famine twice who was no problem at all. I made my way to the altar, smiled,
and sacrified the Amulet...

